      "sha256": "15ecb336f065d40e7a127daf143ac1d817decad0c205214a98658188a417cdfe",
      "lines": [
        {
          "number": 7,
          "content": "RadarState gives the effective search bounds, pattern and receiver status. SEARCH_WIDE and SEARCH_EAST name search patterns; use the reported bounds, not the name alone, for geometry.",
          "highlight": false
        },
        {
          "number": 8,
          "content": "Snapshots are valid from timestamp until valid_until (exclusive), unless replaced earlier. Do not carry state across a gap. Clocks are synchronized UTC within 10ms; report windows include human timing uncertainty.",
          "highlight": false
        },
        {
          "number": 9,
          "content": "InitialReport and RepeatPassReport are human reports from the exercise coordinator. Their position and time uncertainty are explicit. The exercise target identifier need not be present in radar observations. A spatial match is not independent identity confirmation.",
          "highlight": true
        },
        {
          "number": 10,
          "content": "Detection/TargetTrack absence is meaningful only within an interval with complete message-type, all-target, spatially unfiltered capture and zero recorder drops. Partial exports cannot prove absence.",
          "highlight": false
        },
        {
          "number": 11,
          "content": "Use inspect_region with a report badge for reproducible geometry, coverage and counts. Its calculation_citation opens the result, method and input references. Use that real calculation handle for derived claims; do not invent a source row. Use reconstruct_state for a UTC instant and trace_request for request identifiers.",
          "highlight": false
        }
      ]
    },
